  "title": "Daoism",
  "summary": "Daoism goes back to China's Warring States period (476–221 BC). Its two classical texts, the Laozi and the Zhuangzi, emerged between the fifth and third centuries BC, and historians first coined the category of Daoist during the Han. It grew from folk religion in rural China and became the official religion under the Tang dynasty, so it is both a philosophy and a religion. It stresses acting naturally, in accordance with the Dao.",
